<article class="env-lemma" id="014O">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/014O">Lemma <span data-tag="014O">13.9.17</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an additive category. Let $f : K^\bullet \to L^\bullet $ be a morphism of complexes. The triangle $(L^\bullet , C(f)^\bullet , K^\bullet [1], i, p, f[1])$ is the triangle associated to the termwise split sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to L^\bullet \to C(f)^\bullet \to K^\bullet [1] \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> coming from the definition of the cone of $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>